  "worked_solution": "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x)^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+{x}^{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x \\\\  & =2x(\\operatorname{sinh}⁡2x+x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
